WEBVTT

00:10.880 --> 00:12.710
This is how I'll become...

00:15.710 --> 00:17.460
This is how I'll become...

00:19.580 --> 00:21.250
...Supreme Commander.

00:21.630 --> 00:22.710
...a hero.

00:23.330 --> 00:25.000
This is my story!

02:10.210 --> 02:12.460
Dammit! They just keep coming!

02:11.920 --> 02:15.710
<b>United Front, Tenka, Soar</b>

02:16.540 --> 02:17.710
I've got this!

02:26.080 --> 02:28.040
Nice one, Commander!

02:30.750 --> 02:32.380
BOOM!

02:33.210 --> 02:34.380
Wha-bam!

02:43.920 --> 02:45.960
I'm displeased!

02:46.380 --> 02:50.540
I waited patiently,
yet only two targets came out to play.

02:50.540 --> 02:52.420
Where are the rest of you?

02:52.670 --> 02:55.580
Two targets, myself included...

02:55.580 --> 02:57.880
Is he after us commanders?

02:58.170 --> 03:01.960
This battle will be over
in the blink of an eye!

03:11.420 --> 03:14.210
THAT was their leader? Ridiculous.

03:14.210 --> 03:17.420
I should've expected as much from a pest!

03:22.750 --> 03:25.210
If you could stay still, that'd be great.

03:25.420 --> 03:27.580
A pest, attempting to kick me?

03:27.580 --> 03:29.210
Such arrogance!

03:29.210 --> 03:32.830
Besides, my flesh is as strong as steel!

03:34.040 --> 03:35.500
I am invincible!

03:47.210 --> 03:49.130
She wounded me?

03:50.000 --> 03:51.290
Incredible!

03:52.080 --> 03:53.710
She's taking on a humanoid!

03:53.710 --> 03:56.000
Yeah, Lady Ten's talented like that!

03:56.000 --> 03:59.080
She could escape anything
'cause of her ability, even an ambush.

03:59.080 --> 04:01.330
But she doesn't need to run away!

04:01.830 --> 04:05.170
Both commanders came up with a plan to
wipe out an invading army in no time flat,

04:05.170 --> 04:08.040
and they did it all in their heads!

04:08.920 --> 04:10.290
Lady Ten! Lady Kyou!

04:10.290 --> 04:11.790
You're so awesome!

04:11.790 --> 04:15.000
P-please don't shake me so hard!

04:15.250 --> 04:17.460
Impudent brat!

04:17.460 --> 04:18.960
Fine!

04:20.500 --> 04:22.920
This time, I'll simply have to...

04:23.130 --> 04:25.330
blow you to smithereens!

04:32.830 --> 04:34.710
Good luck avoiding that one!

04:37.080 --> 04:38.880
Wha-?! Is she...?

04:38.880 --> 04:40.460
Relax.

04:40.670 --> 04:41.960
The end.

04:45.630 --> 04:47.500
Did you think it was over?

04:57.040 --> 04:59.460
She teleported me with a touch?!

05:05.380 --> 05:07.460
The perfect position.

05:08.420 --> 05:12.330
Lady Ten has the godlike ability
to manipulate the space around her!

05:12.330 --> 05:13.500
And it's aptly named!

05:14.080 --> 05:15.540
Ame-no-Mitori.

05:16.000 --> 05:17.920
<b>AME-NO-MITORI</b>

05:32.420 --> 05:34.500
If I rip apart the fabric of space,

05:34.500 --> 05:37.040
your defenses don't
do you much good, do they?

05:38.330 --> 05:41.290
An entire swarm of Shuuki, gone!

05:41.290 --> 05:43.920
All of the commanders are like that.

05:43.920 --> 05:46.130
They're obviously on a different level.

05:46.580 --> 05:50.790
And Miss Kyouka wants to be the
Supreme Commander in charge of them?

05:50.790 --> 05:53.250
Sounds like an awfully ambitious goal...

05:56.040 --> 06:00.210
True, but I'm going to be
the next Supreme Commander!

06:01.420 --> 06:03.420
Guess I don't have to worry...

06:03.880 --> 06:06.500
Alright, ladies, hunt down
the stragglers and take them out.

06:06.500 --> 06:07.580
Yes, ma'am!

06:10.130 --> 06:12.790
I can't just stand around gawking
at Miss Kyouka.

06:12.790 --> 06:16.210
I made up my mind!
To be a hero here in Mato!

06:25.830 --> 06:27.630
We exterminated the Shuuki army,

06:27.830 --> 06:31.960
but according to Nei's report,
there were other enemy generals present.

06:31.960 --> 06:34.210
And yet there was no sign of them.

06:34.210 --> 06:37.630
We searched every nook and cranny,
but still came up emptyhanded.

06:37.790 --> 06:41.080
What if all of 'em got squashed
in that big blast?

06:41.210 --> 06:42.750
I'm not so sure.

06:42.750 --> 06:45.040
They were very peculiar...

06:45.210 --> 06:46.960
Sorry, everyone...

06:46.960 --> 06:51.960
Even with the power of foresight,
I detected the enemy too late...

06:52.710 --> 06:54.080
Hey, it happens.

06:54.080 --> 06:56.830
They probably have
some sort of cloaking ability.

06:56.830 --> 06:59.630
You detected them before they attacked us.

06:59.630 --> 07:03.210
In other words,
you thwarted any potential for an ambush.

07:03.420 --> 07:06.580
That's all you need to know,
so don't dwell on it.

07:06.580 --> 07:07.960
Precisely.

07:07.960 --> 07:09.170
'Kay!

07:10.040 --> 07:11.170
Little slave.

07:11.630 --> 07:13.790
You really stole the show out there.

07:13.790 --> 07:15.830
Oh, I dunno about that...

07:15.830 --> 07:18.630
You were way more impressive than me,
Miss Izumo!

07:19.330 --> 07:20.420
Mr. Yuuki!

07:20.790 --> 07:23.290
I saw your performance
out on the battlefield!

07:23.290 --> 07:26.250
Now I know that boys
can be talented sometimes, too!

07:26.250 --> 07:29.000
If ya don't mind,
can I have your autograph?!

07:29.000 --> 07:29.880
ME?!

07:29.880 --> 07:31.960
See? You've got a fan.

07:32.080 --> 07:33.250
Hey, uh...

07:33.960 --> 07:35.040
Whaddya want?

07:35.040 --> 07:36.420
About earlier...

07:39.460 --> 07:41.420
Thanks a lot for saving me.

07:43.710 --> 07:46.290
Yes, well, you ARE an Azuma.

07:46.290 --> 07:49.420
Letting the enemy defeat you
would bring shame upon the family!

07:49.420 --> 07:51.670
That's why I saved you.
That's the only reason!

07:52.000 --> 07:55.580
Of course, if you're saying that you felt
the weight of your own inadequacies,

07:55.580 --> 07:57.540
I'd graciously train them out of you!

07:57.540 --> 07:59.420
So why not come back home and-

08:00.630 --> 08:03.080
The 7th Squadron is my home.

08:05.330 --> 08:08.380
Writing up a report
is going be a challenge...

08:08.380 --> 08:10.000
As for the exhibition match...

08:10.000 --> 08:12.750
Mhm. I suppose we'll call it
a draw for now.

08:12.750 --> 08:14.170
It's unfortunate...

08:14.170 --> 08:16.460
I was looking forward
to our little one-on-one.

08:16.460 --> 08:17.960
Me, too.

08:18.630 --> 08:20.380
Well, we're heading out now.

08:20.380 --> 08:22.080
Bye-bye!

08:23.580 --> 08:24.670
Later.

08:31.920 --> 08:33.460
I'm beat!

08:33.460 --> 08:35.710
I need a nice, refreshing bath!

08:38.130 --> 08:39.380
Is this...

08:40.130 --> 08:41.960
supposed to be my reward?

08:41.960 --> 08:44.750
Weren't you the one who asked for this?!

08:45.380 --> 08:46.630
So indecent...

08:46.630 --> 08:49.540
Well, he did slay
a substantial number of Shuuki today...

08:50.710 --> 08:52.250
Miss Kyouka, too?!

08:52.250 --> 08:54.290
I get both at the same time?!

08:54.290 --> 08:56.330
The price of my ability...

08:56.330 --> 08:57.880
Every single time...

08:57.880 --> 08:59.750
Yet somehow I'm always surprised.

09:00.000 --> 09:01.210
She's...

09:01.210 --> 09:06.290
going to get in
the hot spring with me?!

09:06.290 --> 09:07.830
You pervert.

09:08.080 --> 09:09.540
Take off your damn clothes!

09:09.540 --> 09:11.130
O-on it!

09:18.880 --> 09:22.460
I wasn't sure what to expect
when we stripped naked all of a sudden...

09:22.460 --> 09:24.790
Evidently, he wanted a good scrub-down.

09:24.790 --> 09:28.080
I just thought it'd be nice to freshen up.

09:28.210 --> 09:30.210
Well, it's basically the same
as bathing an obedient dog,

09:30.210 --> 09:32.130
so there's no reason to
be embarrassed about it!

09:32.130 --> 09:34.460
I can't understand you
when you talk that fast...

09:36.630 --> 09:40.380
Yuuki, you're more tired
than usual, aren't you?

09:41.250 --> 09:42.420
Yeah...

09:42.420 --> 09:45.080
Two masters at once took a lot out of me.

09:45.080 --> 09:49.290
So it makes you strong,
but it's not to be used lightly...

09:49.500 --> 09:51.960
We learned to utilize Slave
in a practical way.

09:51.960 --> 09:55.920
And we'll need to continue exploring
its potential in the future.

09:57.250 --> 09:59.960
But for the time being,
you should get some rest.

10:00.420 --> 10:02.920
The dorm's hot spring
is great for curing fatigue.

10:14.420 --> 10:17.080
The enemies Nei saw looked just like this!

10:19.670 --> 10:21.670
Amazing as always!

10:22.080 --> 10:23.290
My magnum opus!

10:24.290 --> 10:27.290
Sure, it's good,
but the art style is kind of...

10:28.040 --> 10:31.500
They'll make an
official composite sketch at HQ later.

10:32.630 --> 10:36.380
Neither of them are the humanoid
we encountered last time.

10:48.960 --> 10:51.290
The one that looks like my sister...

10:51.290 --> 10:53.790
How come she wasn't with them?

10:53.790 --> 10:56.250
Are they just a different squad?

10:56.540 --> 11:00.710
Or is there... some other reason?

11:20.040 --> 11:22.960
<b>To Miss Ginna Bizen</b>

11:20.040 --> 11:22.960
<b>7th Squadron</b>

11:20.040 --> 11:22.960
<b>Yuuki Wakura</b>

11:38.000 --> 11:40.750
So this is the 6th Squadron's dorm...

11:40.750 --> 11:42.880
I first noticed when
we visited the 5th Squadron,

11:42.880 --> 11:46.040
but all of the dormitories
look identical on the outside.

11:46.040 --> 11:47.710
For the most part, yes.

11:47.710 --> 11:50.630
Though they tend to differ slightly
in terms of the interior.

11:52.380 --> 11:54.290
Come on in, you three!

11:54.290 --> 11:56.130
Thanks for making the trek.

11:56.130 --> 11:58.130
A little change of scenery never hurt.

11:59.380 --> 12:01.580
Run into any trouble on your way over?

12:01.580 --> 12:04.960
Took down some Shuuki en route,
but that's it.

12:04.960 --> 12:07.330
It's business as usual with Mato itself.

12:09.880 --> 12:11.960
Tenka and I need to have a meeting.

12:11.960 --> 12:16.500
In the meantime, Himari, I want you to get
properly acquainted with the 6th Squadron.

12:16.500 --> 12:18.710
Some of our members
went out on an expedition,

12:18.710 --> 12:20.420
so they won't be joining us.

12:20.420 --> 12:24.500
But the rest are here in the dorm,
so feel free to take a look around.

12:24.500 --> 12:25.420
Thank you.

12:25.670 --> 12:27.750
As we discussed this morning, Yuuki...

12:27.750 --> 12:28.630
Yes, ma'am.

12:28.630 --> 12:29.830
As the squad's caretaker,

12:29.830 --> 12:32.130
I ought to help out
while we're here, right?

12:32.380 --> 12:33.500
I'm sorry.

12:33.500 --> 12:36.130
Our caretaker isn't home at the moment.

12:36.130 --> 12:39.460
They'll be back this evening,
so it's just until then.

12:39.460 --> 12:40.790
Not a problem.

12:40.790 --> 12:44.540
As part of the Demon Defense Force,
we've gotta have each other's backs!

12:44.540 --> 12:47.500
Right. I'm counting on you.

12:49.880 --> 12:51.040
Yes, ma'am!

12:51.250 --> 12:52.580
Leave it to me!

12:55.670 --> 12:58.130
All right! Step one: Cleaning!

13:01.460 --> 13:06.040
Or it would be,
but this place is pretty clean already.

13:07.710 --> 13:10.000
And here I was getting all amped up.

13:12.420 --> 13:14.000
This stain...

13:14.960 --> 13:19.630
Judging by the feel of it, Formula 5 might
work better than plain old baking soda...

13:20.580 --> 13:22.250
Or maybe...

13:22.960 --> 13:25.080
So many choices!

13:25.670 --> 13:27.540
Next up is laundry!

13:33.130 --> 13:35.790
Breathe... Just calm down...

13:36.130 --> 13:39.380
You do the 7th Squadron's laundry
all the time!

13:40.960 --> 13:43.080
Never mind... I'm still not used to it!

13:43.080 --> 13:45.040
<b>7TH SQUADRON</b>

13:46.250 --> 13:49.130
Wonder what Yukki's up to right now...

13:49.630 --> 13:52.380
I wish I could've gone with him...

13:57.580 --> 14:00.420
No, I told myself I'd get him
to like me more!

14:00.420 --> 14:04.080
If anything, I should be using this time
for self-improvement!

14:04.080 --> 14:05.080
Yeah!

14:07.330 --> 14:10.250
Guess I'll start... by tidying up...

14:10.250 --> 14:12.210
<b>6TH SQUADRON</b>

14:14.750 --> 14:17.500
Himari's big sister's room...

14:14.750 --> 14:17.460
<b>Yachiho Azuma</b>

14:22.540 --> 14:24.920
I wonder what she'll say if she sees me...

14:27.710 --> 14:29.830
Anyone home?

14:31.830 --> 14:33.290
Hello?

14:35.580 --> 14:37.080
She's not here.

14:37.080 --> 14:39.500
Guess I'll just leave this in her room.

14:40.130 --> 14:41.500
Pardon the intrusion-

15:00.080 --> 15:02.500
Oh my god! Oh my god! Oh my god!
Oh my god! Oh my god!

15:02.500 --> 15:04.290
OH MY GOD!

15:11.210 --> 15:13.170
Miss Sahara Wakasa?!

15:13.920 --> 15:16.040
Why is she asleep in the living room?!

15:16.040 --> 15:18.750
And in her underwear, no less!

15:19.920 --> 15:22.250
Can't let her catch a cold...

15:22.250 --> 15:23.580
So I'll just...

15:25.960 --> 15:26.830
Wha-?!

15:31.380 --> 15:33.790
Does she think I'm her pillow?!

15:35.250 --> 15:38.580
I-I have to bail before someone sees!

15:40.420 --> 15:43.000
You're not going anywhere...

15:43.000 --> 15:44.540
O-oh yeah...

15:44.540 --> 15:47.500
This is the girl who wrestled like a pro
in the exhibition match!

15:47.500 --> 15:50.210
Either way, I've gotta get free!

15:50.580 --> 15:53.580
Now behave yourself...!

15:57.290 --> 16:00.080
And though I wished for escape,
I was unable to escape.

16:00.080 --> 16:03.580
So eventually, I stopped thinking.

16:04.170 --> 16:07.040
<b>BOOM</b>

16:04.170 --> 16:07.040
<b>And though he wished for escape, he was unable to escape.</b>

16:04.170 --> 16:07.040
<b>So eventually, Yuuki stopped thinking.</b>

16:07.960 --> 16:10.250
Aw jeez, my bad!

16:10.500 --> 16:14.460
I forgot the 7th Squadron
was supposed to come visit today!

16:14.460 --> 16:15.540
Yeah...

16:18.880 --> 16:20.960
What's the matter, Himari?

16:20.960 --> 16:23.460
I'm waiting until she's done
to speak to her.

16:40.710 --> 16:42.750
Does Yachiho do this on a regular basis?

16:42.750 --> 16:43.790
Mhm.

16:43.790 --> 16:46.380
She trained like that
before the exhibition match, too.

16:47.130 --> 16:49.960
She's pushing herself
even harder nowadays...

16:51.080 --> 16:55.670
Hey, Himari, do you look up to Yacchi?

16:57.460 --> 17:00.000
Her personality sucks...

17:00.000 --> 17:03.130
but she does well
academically and athletically,

17:03.130 --> 17:05.960
so I've always thought I could stand
to learn a thing or two from her.

17:06.380 --> 17:07.790
Personally,

17:07.790 --> 17:12.130
I'm a fan of the theory that
someone's Peach ability is based on

17:12.130 --> 17:13.920
their nature and knowledge.

17:14.460 --> 17:17.500
So in your case, Himari,
your desire to learn from Yacchi

17:17.500 --> 17:20.330
is what became your ability!

17:20.540 --> 17:23.540
Same goes for Yacchi's ability
to control time.

17:24.040 --> 17:27.290
It stems from her desire
to spend time with her little sister.

17:27.290 --> 17:29.250
Makes sense, don'tcha think?

17:31.210 --> 17:33.830
I-I think that's a huge stretch!

17:33.830 --> 17:38.170
Aw, but it might be nice
if you talk to her a little more often!

17:38.170 --> 17:39.170
Right?

17:39.170 --> 17:41.130
Huh? Oh, yeah!

17:41.380 --> 17:43.500
Your big sister's cool!

17:43.500 --> 17:44.630
Here.

17:47.750 --> 17:49.170
Yeah, I guess...

18:03.960 --> 18:05.040
Wha-?!

18:05.040 --> 18:07.330
The least you can do is say thanks!

18:07.330 --> 18:09.710
Mm, sorry. Can't hear you.

18:10.170 --> 18:10.500
Um, check your attitude!

18:10.500 --> 18:11.830
What a relief!
Um, check your attitude!<b></b>

18:11.830 --> 18:14.250
They're getting along better already.

18:14.250 --> 18:15.080
Yeah.

18:15.080 --> 18:17.670
Although I suppose
showing her Yacchi's room

18:17.670 --> 18:20.540
would be the most efficient solution.

18:20.540 --> 18:23.210
Perhaps it's best
we keep that part a secret...

18:24.500 --> 18:26.790
Track down the humanoid Shuuki?

18:26.790 --> 18:27.750
Yes.

18:29.580 --> 18:33.170
We've seen no movement from the humanoids
since this latest attack.

18:33.170 --> 18:36.500
So instead of waiting around,
I think we ought to make the first move.

18:36.920 --> 18:38.460
Yeah, good point...

18:38.460 --> 18:42.130
A few days ago, in that crater where
a large group of Shuuki appeared.

18:42.130 --> 18:44.170
That's when we
first encountered a humanoid.

18:44.170 --> 18:46.420
I think that's where
we should start our investigation.

18:46.580 --> 18:49.290
Okay. I've got no problem with that.

18:49.290 --> 18:53.290
I'm curious as to how many more
of these things exist.

18:53.290 --> 18:55.540
We've confirmed a total of four so far.

18:56.330 --> 18:59.830
But you already eliminated
one of those four, correct?

19:00.040 --> 19:01.330
I'm not certain.

19:01.330 --> 19:05.290
Honestly, I didn't get the vibe
that it was well and truly dead.

19:26.920 --> 19:30.830
Glad to see you've made
a full recovery, Rairen.

19:31.330 --> 19:34.290
That was a seriously close call.

19:47.630 --> 19:49.830
Good thing you have me, huh?

19:50.290 --> 19:52.540
I could have kept fighting after that!

19:54.380 --> 19:58.790
The battle was lost when you let them
raze your Shuuki army to the ground.

19:58.790 --> 20:01.130
I agree with Shikoku's assessment.

20:02.380 --> 20:04.540
Let's review, shall we?

20:04.830 --> 20:09.170
First, in order to evaluate the enemy's
capabilities, I fought the 3rd Squadron.

20:09.170 --> 20:11.000
It was a piece of cake,

20:11.000 --> 20:13.040
but their commander
wasn't with them at the time.

20:13.500 --> 20:15.380
So the purpose of this recent endeavor

20:15.380 --> 20:18.210
was to experience
a commander's strength firsthand...

20:18.460 --> 20:21.540
But they blew my expectations
out of the water.

20:21.880 --> 20:24.750
Therefore, your plan to
"make use of our current resources

20:24.750 --> 20:27.630
and launch a full-scale
attack on the Demon Defense Force"

20:27.630 --> 20:28.750
is garbage!

20:28.750 --> 20:30.460
Wait just a second!

20:30.460 --> 20:34.250
They may be tough for a bunch of pests,
but they can be beaten!

20:34.250 --> 20:37.580
Which of us
do you think is right, Jouryuu?!

20:37.920 --> 20:39.250
Shikoku.

20:39.960 --> 20:41.170
That hurts...

20:41.170 --> 20:44.710
Now that that's settled,
we're going with my plan this time.

20:45.040 --> 20:48.380
We'll attack once we've gathered
all eight people.

20:48.380 --> 20:50.670
Until then, we operate from the shadows.

20:52.210 --> 20:54.710
The eight of us
will be together soon enough...

20:54.710 --> 20:56.130
Alright, fine.

20:56.420 --> 20:57.580
However...!

20:57.580 --> 21:00.420
I despise the phrase "eight people"!

21:00.420 --> 21:04.540
We are NOT "people"!
Don't treat us like we're humans!

21:05.420 --> 21:06.750
My mistake!

21:07.000 --> 21:10.210
You're interested in the humans,
aren't you, Shikoku?

21:10.920 --> 21:13.250
Humans are entertaining!

21:13.500 --> 21:17.420
You might say they're more...
complex than I imagined.

21:17.420 --> 21:19.380
I just can't get enough.

21:19.790 --> 21:22.080
I suppose that concludes today's meeting.

21:24.000 --> 21:25.540
Was there anything else?

21:26.170 --> 21:28.750
Just one thing, regarding personnel.

21:28.920 --> 21:30.130
What is it?

21:33.080 --> 21:35.540
May I have the little slave?

23:11.000 --> 23:13.460
<b>TEACH US! NEI-SENPAI!</b>

23:11.380 --> 23:12.920
"Teach Us! Nei-senpai!"

23:12.920 --> 23:13.580
Okey-dokey!

23:13.460 --> 23:18.210
<b>MEMBERS ONLY FIGHTING ARENA: GINNA'S CLUB</b>

23:13.580 --> 23:16.080
Today we're talking about Miss Ginna Bizen
from the 10th Squadron

23:16.080 --> 23:17.500
and her Peach ability, Ginna's Club!

23:17.500 --> 23:20.330
This ability allows Miss Ginna
to erect a powerful barrier within

23:20.330 --> 23:22.880
the boundaries established
by lines drawn on the ground,

23:22.880 --> 23:25.830
and only those who sign their names
can enter the barrier.

23:25.830 --> 23:27.960
She can heal the wounds of anyone inside
the barrier,

23:27.960 --> 23:29.290
which means she's always in high demand

23:29.290 --> 23:32.210
for things like combat simulation training
and Mato intersquad exhibition matches!

23:32.330 --> 23:34.670
As a side note, Miss Ginna is a big fan
of the Demon Defense Force,

23:32.500 --> 23:36.830
<b>Kyouka Uzen</b>

23:34.670 --> 23:36.920
and she enjoys collecting
the autographs of its members!

23:36.920 --> 23:37.830
Anyways, next time:

23:37.500 --> 23:40.960
<b>PROMISE,</b>

23:37.500 --> 23:40.960
<b>NEI,</b>

23:37.500 --> 23:40.960
<b>REMEMBER</b>

23:37.830 --> 23:39.380
